AUDIO: 'are at 1200 and 1500 nits, respectively, meaning you\'ll better be able to see them in bright conditions. We\'re also getting a really, really good 12 hours of battery life as well as four microphones and speakers to take calls and listen to music. And you\'ll also'

[01:54] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'notice the logo on the side with the classic smart glasses touchpad for controlling the glasses. And you might notice there\'s no camera, which is part of their privacy first focus, which some people love, some people hate. So, it just really depends on who you are. But'

[02:06] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'they can pull off great features by focusing their efforts away from the camera. I think that can work really well. Other glasses have done that really well. But does it work well in these? Let\'s just see. As far as controls, you can swipe forward and backward to navigate the menus. You can tap to select, double tap to go back.'

[02:19] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'You can also hold the action button on the top right to activate holiday AI. You can press and hold the bottom arm to turn on and off the glasses. And you can press once on the bottom arm to turn on and off the screen. So, first we got to'

[02:31] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'talk about the style. And they look pretty dang good in my opinion. I love that they don\'t look like every other pair of smart glasses like the Wayfairer style or the headliner style which most smart glasses tend to look like these days. like that\'s kind of a unique'

[02:44] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'combination without being like crazy weird or anything. Like the style has been something that they\'ve tried to focus on in the past which I think is really cool. But I know you guys are dying to know the actual features and the biggest of those that I\'ll talk about first is this one feature called'

[02:57] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'meeting flow which is basically a bunch of features in one. It could potentially really change the way you have conversations and meetings. So one thing you can do before you even set up this feature you can go into the settings you can turn on live captions which is really nice for the entire conversation.'

[03:10] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'That way you\'re getting captions. Also, if it happens to be an entire meeting in another language, you can set the language of that and get live translation. I\'ve tested live translation separately. You can also do it as a separate feature. It doesn\'t have to be within the meeting and it'

[03:22] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'works pretty well. You can even set it to show the original language and the new language on the screen so that you can even learn some of the new language if you want. Now, let\'s get into the actual meeting flow because honestly, it\'s kind of insane. So, I tested this with Val here. We had a pretty long'

[03:35] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'conversation, talked about numerous different things. Now, let me talk about my favorite thing in this entire experience. So number one, you\'re talking. You\'re getting all the live captions as the conversation\'s happening. And you\'re doing this line by line. It\'s not going to show a bunch of'

[03:47] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'them. It\'s going to show one line at a time. You can open the phone app, go into the meeting live, and see the entire transcript of the entire conversation. Scroll up and down if you wish. Now, along with these captions, you might remember something from like the even G2s where they have this'

[03:59] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'conversate feature. And even the holiday G1s had something like this where it would listen to the conversations happening around you and it would give you suggestions for things relevant to that conversation. So if someone starts talking about Albert Einstein, might'

[04:11] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'tell you who he is, give you some facts about him. There\'s a question brought up that no one knows the answer to, it might pull up the answer for you in the glasses. Does that stuff automatically the problem with that in those last two pairs of glasses is because it was automatic, it didn\'t always register and you didn\'t always get the info you'

[04:24] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'needed. Sometimes it worked, sometimes it just didn\'t activate. But that\'s completely changed because you can set a long press of the touchpad. So you just tap and hold on the side for a second to either quick research or quick summary. Now quick research is what I think is super cool. in the middle of your'

[04:37] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'conversation. If someone brings up a question, no one knows the answer to it. They\'re talking about something interesting and you you don\'t know what it is. You can just tap and hold on the side. I did this numerous times during the conversation and then it will bring things up manually about what you were talking about. It\'ll do the research for'

[04:49] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'you, tell you something about what you\'re talking about at that moment in time. This prevents it missing crucial things or you wanted to suggest something that will help the conversation and it just doesn\'t register or activate because you can just tap and hold on the side and it will just do it manually for you on the'

[05:02] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'spot. you can decide which things you want. You research during the middle of the conversation or meeting. It\'s it\'s kind of great. Use this multiple times and most of the time it worked pretty dang well. So, we recently watched The Odyssey, the 2026 film, and we were talking about like what actors are in it'

[05:15] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'or like who played this person and like what else were they in? We talked about other different actors and I was able to pull up stuff on the spot and add more things to that conversation. Now, there is a slight delay based on basically your Wi-Fi. So, if you\'re having a one-on-one conversation, you might have'

[05:28] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'to wait a second or two just like with Conversate or any of the other glasses. But this really thrives when one, you\'re not in a rush in your one-on-one conversation, but two, when you\'re in a conversation with more than one person. Like, everyone\'s around you can recognize the entire thing, and you can'

[05:41] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'add other things or understand other things that you otherwise would just have to either pull your phone out and Google, which is kind of rude sometimes. Definitely can\'t really do that in meetings or you\'ll have to just look it up later after the meeting. And with this, you can do it in the middle. You'

[05:53] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'can also swipe and switch between quick research and quick summary. It will summarize what you\'re talking about at that current moment. So if you space out for instance, you can just tap quick summary and it will just tell you everything that was happening in that time frame, which is really cool. So for'

[06:06] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'all you guys who space out, that\'s a really useful feature. Use that a couple times and it does the job. Now it\'s not going to summarize the entire meeting. You can actually go into your phone and look at all your quick summaries, all your quick research during the meeting. And at the end of the meeting or'

[06:18] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'conversation, it\'s going to give you the entire transcript, all the research things you did, all the summaries you pulled up, and a grand summary of the entire thing. It\'ll also auto add things like to-do list. So we also talked about what our plans were for the day. So, it told me that I had to film and edit this'

[06:31] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'video today and the due date for it and then also had an open conversation, which I think is really cool. We brought up the question of smart glasses and like what they are and then we kind of got distracted, started talking about something else. So, in the actual summary, it tells us, oh, you guys'

[06:43] [scene:talk]
